{"Title":"An Act to remove HCA real estate barriers to equitable participation in the cannabis industry","BillNumber":"H124","DocketNumber":"HD3958","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"C_T1","Name":"Chynah Tyler","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_T1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T15:41:26.907"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"C_T1","Name":"Chynah Tyler","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_T1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T15:41:26.9066667"},{"Id":"L_S1","Name":"Lindsay N. Sabadosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_S1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T12:17:47.66"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H124/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Tyler of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 124) of Chynah Tyler and Lindsay N. Sabadosa for legislation to remove host community agreement real estate barriers to equitable participation in the cannabis industry.  Cannabis Policy.","DocumentText":"\tSubsection (a½) of section 4 of chapter 94G, as amended by Chapter 180 of the Acts of 2022so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out clauses (xxxi) and inserting in place thereof the following clauses:-\r\n\t(xxxi)  establish procedures and policies for municipalities to promote and encourage full participation in the regulated marijuana industry during negotiations of host community agreements with social equity program businesses and economic empowerment priority applicants, including policies and procedures that enable such businesses to obtain host community agreements without requiring a signed lease or real estate letter of intent; and\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J50","Ge